			"reason": "Independently compared all 36 public declarations, comprising 21 theorems and 15 definitions, and all 24 reachable local definitions with the frozen Lean sources, elaborated exports, supplied blind readback and stated contract. The carrier is Polynomial ℝ; spans are algebraic spans of finite combinations. Both high families use every natural m≥2. Natural exponent subtraction is truncated, while the coefficient denominator uses real subtraction; m≥2 prevents its vanishing. The augmented-span proof handles the low-degree bases explicitly and uses even/odd induction followed by polynomial induction, establishing the universal claim without degree sampling. Sparse-span inclusion in the residual kernel and residues(X²)=(2,−2) establish X² exclusion. The four-trace map genuinely evaluates the two endpoint residuals of p and D²p. Independent exact rational calculations confirmed its X²,…,X⁵ columns, determinant 15360 and both inverse identities. The source proves the LinearMap right-inverse identity for every real four-vector, zero corrected traces for every real polynomial, and kernel fixation under the explicit zero-trace hypothesis. The cancellation polynomial is X⁶−5X⁴+7X² with zero four-trace vector, whereas p_even(2) has vector (0,0,24,−24). The five coordinate-detection equalities use the actual real Euclidean inner product. The compound root has no outer hypotheses and contains substantive, nonvacuous assertions. No hidden analytic premise, trivial replacement definition or narrowing beyond the expressly declared real-algebra scope was found.",
